# `Scala3` code example

It is assumed that you have a recent version of `scala3`, its `sbt` package manager and a `jvm`
installed. The generated code has a dependency on the Apache Kafka client jar.

We run the examples directly via `sbt`. First we will list all Kafka topics that we have access to.

```shell
> cd {{proxy-name}}-example-scala3
> sbt "runMain org.kpn.dsh.proxy.{{proxy-name-underscore}}.ListTopics"
...
scratch.my-topic.{{tenant}}
...
```

Then we will send messages to a Kafka topic. In the example below we use topic
`scratch.my-topic.{{tenant}}`. Use `ctrl-c` to stop the program.

```shell
> sbt "runMain org.kpn.dsh.proxy.{{proxy-name-underscore}}.Producer scratch.my-topic.{{tenant}}"
{{proxy-name}}-producer-scala3: 1780047895
{{proxy-name}}-producer-scala3: 1780047896
{{proxy-name}}-producer-scala3: 1780047897
{{proxy-name}}-producer-scala3: 1780047898
^C
```

Next we will consume records from the same topic. Again, use `ctrl-c` to stop the program.

```shell
> sbt "runMain org.kpn.dsh.proxy.{{proxy-name-underscore}}.Consumer scratch.my-topic.{{tenant}}"
0:2808 {{proxy-name}}-producer-scala3: 1780047895
0:2809 {{proxy-name}}-producer-scala3: 1780047896
0:2810 {{proxy-name}}-producer-scala3: 1780047897
0:2811 {{proxy-name}}-producer-scala3: 1780047898
^C
```
